{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfuY6myH4vyJ6Aw4mjNbg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I ruled the TC-055 amendment **MEANING** (1 row) and, because the TC rung is released, re-attested it myself.\n\n**Verdict** (`f7ab2017c`, trailer `WI: WI-823`, file `docs/reviews/wi-823/001-ADJUDICATE-bc886f2.md`):\n\n- `[MEANING] TC-055 Method`: the new text adds two obligations, both in this one cell:\n  1. **A bigger judge brief.** The judge must now also receive the scope lines and TC ids of every test-bound row behind a live anchor. A brief that was correct under the old text, with only the rubric, intent and shots, fails the new one.\n  2. **A stop rule.** No judgment may be made on a failed shot run or an incomplete matrix. The old text allowed a verdict on a run that missed a tab the page renders, such as Retired, which wasn't in the old `TABS` list.\n- `VERDICT: MEANING rows=1`\n\n**Would I bless the new text?** Yes:\n- **It fits the chain.** SR-054 limits the judged part to the one clause no test holds, and LLR-055 keeps only what a test cannot pin. Giving the judge the scope lines of the tests that own each anchor's core is what keeps a verdict from re-ruling a tested clause. TC-055's own Expected cell already requires that.\n- **Both new terms can be checked.** The live anchor set comes from the rubric, which Expected names as its single home. \"Incomplete\" is measured against the tabs the page renders, and `shoot.mjs` prints any it missed as `NOT shot`.\n\n**Re-attestation** (`2af374645`, separate commit): `python project-trajectory/scripts/intake.py --root . snapshot --reattests TC-055` recorded act 105 with `reattested = [\"TC-055\"]`. Nothing was refused. Only TC-055's Method moved in the anchor, and the anchor copy now matches the live `test-cases.toml` byte for byte. The commit's checks passed (`RESULT: PASS`); the `check_trajectory` WARNs it printed are about other LLRs, not this change. I edited no registry cell.\n\n**For the coordinator:**\n- **LLR-055's child list is out of date.** Its detail names only the T2/T3/T1 child rows. The rubric also binds T4 (LLR-119), T5 (LLR-105, LLR-285) and T8 (LLR-120, LLR-292). As you said, this predates the lane. It didn't block the ruling, because the new Method reads that set from the rubric, not from LLR-055.\n- **Untracked file left alone.** `docs/reviews/wi-823/001-ADJUDICATE-bc886f2.md.requested` still says `outcome = pending`. I took it to be your request marker, so I neither committed nor edited it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1588,"cache_read_input_tokens":60661,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1588},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0352a375-be9f-4836-bcc4-e389f08eec57","uuid":"58f981db-c60e-4fde-b154-ba6fea223d80","timestamp":"2026-10-11T00:54:17.267Z","request_id":"req_011CfuY6mhtfBLYNp9BbP6AJ"}
